    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0458" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/899.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to the Department’s telegram of March 20. Minister of Foreign affairs
                    after a consultation with the President informs me that the Haitian Government
                    is anxious to have Consul Livingston aid in arranging for cessation of
                    hostilities with Theodore but states that the Haitian Government cannot make
                    formal request for the Government of the United States to do so. The private
                    secretary of the President has twice called on me and requested in the name of
                    the President that Consul Livingston be instructed to act in this matter in
                    conjunction with Minister Zamor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
